S4: Stanford Stratified Structure Solver (http://fan.group.stanford.edu/S4/)

A program for computing electromagnetic fields in periodic, layered
structures, developed by Victor Liu (victorliu@alumni.stanford.edu) of the
Fan group in the Stanford Electrical Engineering Department.

See the S4 manual, in doc/index.html, for a complete
description of the package and its user interface, as well as
installation instructions, the license and copyright, contact
addresses, and other important information.

Python extension on Ubuntu
--------------------------

Install the C/C++ compiler, Python development headers, and BLAS/LAPACK
development packages. For the Lua executable and modules, also install Lua 5.2:

    sudo apt-get install build-essential python3-dev python3-setuptools \
        libblas-dev liblapack-dev

Build and check the Python extension with the same Python interpreter:

    make S4_pyext PYTHON=python3
    python3 -m unittest discover -s testing -p 'test_python_binding.py'

`make S4_pyext` produces an importable `S4` module in this directory. It does
not need NumPy or SciPy. The full `make` target also builds the Lua frontend,
which needs `lua5.2` and `liblua5.2-dev`.
